# `git diff` shows an OpenDocument package as its projection — the cells and paragraphs that
# changed — instead of "Binary files differ". The command it runs is not committed with this
# file, so each clone needs it once (`grind init` sets it in the repository it is run in):
#
#   git config diff.grind.textconv "grind project"
*.ods diff=grind
*.odt diff=grind
